{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The limit expression has the following form:\n\n$\\displaystyle\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\dfrac{f(t+h)-f(t)}{h}$\n\nTherefore, it describes a derivative of a certain function $f$ at a certain $x$-value $t$. Can you recognize what $f$ and $t$ are?","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Since the numerator is $4\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}+h\\right)-4\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$, we can tell that the function is $f(x)=4\\sin(x)$ and the $x$-value is $\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$.\n\nIn other words, the limit expression is equal to $f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$ for $f(x)=4\\sin(x)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's find $f'(x)$:\n\n$f'(x)=4\\cos(x)$\n\nNow let's evaluate $f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$:\n\n$f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=4\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=0$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\displaystyle\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\dfrac{4\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}+h\\right)-4\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)}{h}=0$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Find $\\displaystyle\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\dfrac{4\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}+h\\right)-4\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)}{h}$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$0$","correct":true},{"content":"$1$","correct":false},{"content":"$4$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"The limit doesn't exist","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
